Section 2—Trial Examination
nS
MCQ 2.147
| A 24-year-old woman presents for her annual checkup and Pap smear. Her partner
_ is using condoms for contraception. She has no symptoms suggesting a problem
within her genital tract. Her menstrual cycles are each four weeks long. Her last
menstrual period was two weeks ago. On vaginal examination there is a cystic
swelling, about 4cm in diameter, in the region of her right ovary. Which one of the
following is the most appropriate next step in managment?
A. Advise her that the mass is a physiologic cyst and that no treatment or further
review is required.
B. See her again in six weeks and arrange an ultrasound examination if the cyst is
still present.
C. Advise her that laparoscopic drainage of the cyst is necessary now.
D. Arrange an ultrasound examination now.
E. Arrange a computed tomography (CT) of the pelvic region now.
EE
MCQ 2.148
An 11-year-old boy complains
of sudden onset of pain in the
right side of the scrotum four
hours ago, followed by nausea
and vomiting. On examination,
the right hemiscrotum is red and
swollen as illustrated and acutely
tender, but no other abnormality
is found. Which one of the
following is the most appropriate
next step in management?','{"A":"tibiotic.","B":"Send urine for microscopy, culture and sensitivity.","C":"Arrange an ultrasound of scrotum.","D":"Arrange for a total and differential white cell count.","E":"Arrange for surgical exploration of the scrotum.\n95"}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","supporting_pages":[111],"source_qid":"2.147","duplicate_group_id":"exact-5195642cdac8","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"7cd2f12b31c261cecbd1","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_page":111,"source_qid":"2.147"}],"parser_version":"2.8-residual-resolver-selective-ocr-visual-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"v28_selective_ocr_multi_group","text_method":"v28_selective_ocr","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,'text',NULL,'needs_verification','[]','high','{"record_id":"7cd2f12b31c261cecbd1","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_year":null,"source_page":111,"supporting_pages":[111],"source_qid":"2.147","domain_hint":"Mixed/Unclassified","stem":"Australian Medical Council\nSection 2—Trial Examination\nnS\nMCQ 2.147\n| A 24-year-old woman presents for her annual checkup and Pap smear. Her partner\n_ is using condoms for contraception. She has no symptoms suggesting a problem\nwithin her genital tract. Her menstrual cycles are each four weeks long. Her last\nmenstrual period was two weeks ago. On vaginal examination there is a cystic\nswelling, about 4cm in diameter, in the region of her right ovary. Which one of the\nfollowing is the most appropriate next step in managment?\nA. Advise her that the mass is a physiologic cyst and that no treatment or further\nreview is required.\nB. S