A 51-year-old man sustains burns in a house fire in which he ran back into a burning
room to bring out his daughter. The room was full of acrid smoke from burning clothing.
He was burnt on his face, trunk and arms and the burns were judged partial thickness,
involving 30% of the total body surface area. He speaks in a husky whisper and there
is singeing of his hair and eyebrows. Which one of the following actions should be
undertaken first?','{"A":"Insertion of an intravenous catheter.","B":"Endotracheal intubation.","C":"Silver sulfadiazine dressings to the burnt areas.","D":"Administering systemic antibiotics.","E":"A bolus dose of opiate.\n\nMCQ 3.006\n\nA 45-year-old woman presents with a history of multiple subcutaneous lumps. She\nhas noted them for many years; they do not bother her unduly but are occasionally\npainful. On examination, she has multiple discrete focal lumps beneath the skin\nsurface of various sizes up to 3cm in diameter which are soft and lobulated; some are\nmildly tender. She has about 20 in alll which are situated bilaterally in the upper and\nlower limbs and on the trunk. There are no associated skin lesions and she has been\notherwise in good general health. She can remember her mother having had some\nsimilar lumps removed. Which one of the following is the most likely diagnosis?\n\nbe"}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","supporting_pages":[],"source_qid":"3.004","duplicate_group_id":"exact-5cd65ec7af33","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"729e56d7dbbe76ca032c","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_page":224,"source_qid":"3.004"}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"strict_ocr_tolerant","text_method":"tesseract","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'needs_verification','[]','medium','{"record_id":"729e56d7dbbe76ca032c","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_year":null,"source_page":224,"source_qid":"3.004","domain_hint":"Mixed/Unclassified","stem":"Australian Medical Council\n_ Section 3 - Adult Health and Aged Care\n—__e_———————— ~\nMCQ 3.004\nThe 70-year-old man whose Photograph is shown has had the Painless lesion shown\non his lower lip for the last six months and itis slowly increasing in size. Which one of the\nfollowing is the most likely diagnosis?\n. Herpes zoster.\nHerpes simplex.\n. Squamous cell carcinoma.\n. Basal cell carcinoma.\nMalignant melanoma.\nMCQ 3.005\nA\nB.\nS\nD\nES\nA 51-year-old man sustains burns in a house fire in which he ran back into a burning\nroom to bring out his daughter. The room was full of acrid smoke from burning clothing.\nHe was burnt on his face, trunk and arms and the burns were judged partial thickness,\ninvolving 30% of the total body surface area. He speaks in a husky whisper and there\nis singeing of his hair and eyebrows. Which one of the following actions should be\nundertaken first?","options":{"A":"Insertion of an intravenous catheter.","B":"Endotracheal intubation.","C":"Silver sulfadiazine dressings to the burnt areas.","D":"Administering systemic antibiotics.","E":"A bolus dose of opiate.\n\nMCQ 3.006\n\nA 45-year-old woman presents with a history of multiple subcutaneous lumps. She\nhas noted them for many years; they do not bother her unduly but are occasionally\npainful. On examination, she has multiple discrete focal lumps beneath the skin\nsurface of various sizes up to 3cm in diameter which are soft and lobulated; some are\nmildly tender. She has about 20 in alll which are situated bilaterally in the upper and\nlower limbs and on the trunk. There are no associated skin lesions and she has been\notherwise in good general health. She can remember her mother having had some\nsimilar lumps removed. Which one of the following is the most likely diagnosis?\n\nbe"},"source_answer":null,"source_explanation":null,"source_answer_status":"pending_import","current_answer":null,"current_answer_status":"needs_verification","current_evidence":[],"currentness_risk":"medium","currentness_keywords":["age"],"likely_visual_question":false,"pa