Section 3 — Adult Health and Aged Care
Neurofibromatosis type 1 (Von Recklinghausen disease of nerve).
Adiposis dolorosa (Dercum disease).
. Multiple symmetrical subcutaneous lipomas.
Multiple desmoid tumours.
Multiple epidermoid cysts.
MOQOP>
MCQ 3.007
An 18-year-old youth presents with the
changes shown in the photograph. This
condition has been present for many
weeks and is the sixth acute episode
he has suffered over the previous three
months. Which one of the following
would be the most effective treatment
to offer the patient?
A. Regular salt water bathing of the
toe.
B. Application of an antiseptic
dressing to the edge of the toenail.
. Long-term antibiotic therapy.
Wedge resection of the affected region.
Phenol injection into the affected area.
moO
MCQ 3.008
This is the photograph of the natal cleft region of a
28-year-old man who presented with an intermittently
discharging swelling. The anus is at the bottom
of the picture. The discharge has been offensive
smelling and associated with some pain. Which one
of the following is the most appropriate next step in
management?','{"A":"MRI scan to define the anatomical boundaries of\nthe underlying fistulous tract.","B":"Computed tomography to define the underlying\nabscess cavity.","C":"A prolonged course of antibiotics.","D":"Laying open of the fistula between skin and anal\ncanal.","E":"Excision of the sinus and underlying cavity.\n\n207"}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","supporting_pages":[],"source_qid":"3.007","duplicate_group_id":"exact-a7d1c2fd8e2d","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"ab9ccf44dcd2c584b0e4","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_page":225,"source_qid":"3.007"}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"strict_ocr_tolerant","text_method":"tesseract","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'needs_verification','[]','high','{"record_id":"ab9ccf44dcd2c584b0e4","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_year":null,"source_page":225,"source_qid":"3.007","domain_hint":"Mixed/Unclassified","stem":"Australian Medical Council\nSection 3 — Adult Health and Aged Care\nNeurofibromatosis type 1 (Von Recklinghausen disease of nerve).\nAdiposis dolorosa (Dercum disease).\n. Multiple symmetrical subcutaneous lipomas.\nMultiple desmoid tumours.\nMultiple epidermoid cysts.\nMOQOP>\nMCQ 3.007\nAn 18-year-old youth presents with the\nchanges shown in the photograph. This\ncondition has been present for many\nweeks and is the sixth acute episode\nhe has suffered over the previous three\nmonths. Which one of the following\nwould be the most effective treatment\nto offer the patient?\nA. Regular salt water bathing of the\ntoe.\nB. Application of an antiseptic\ndressing to the edge of the toenail.\n. Long-term antibiotic therapy.\nWedge resection of the affected region.\nPhenol injection into the affected area.\nmoO\nMCQ 3.008\nThis is the photograph of the natal cleft region of a\n28-year-old man who presented with an intermittently\ndischarging swelling. The anus is at the bottom\nof the picture. The discharge has been offensive\nsmelling and associated with some pain. Which one\nof the following is the most appropriate next step in\nmanagement?","options":{"A":"MRI scan to define the anatomical boundaries of\nthe underlying fistulous tract.","B":"Computed tomography to define the underlying\nabscess cavity.","C":"A prolonged course of antibiotics.","D":"Laying open of the fistula between skin and anal\ncanal.","E":"Excision of the sinus and underlying cavity.\n\n207"},"source_answer":null,"source_explanation":null,"source_answer_status":"pending_import","current_answer":null,"current_answer_status":"needs_verification","current_evidence":[],"currentness_risk":"high","currentness_keywords":["age","antibiotic","management","therapy","treatment"],"likely_visual_question":false,"parser_confidence":"high","parser_mode":"strict_ocr_tolerant","text_method":"tesseract","parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","stem_hash":"a7d1c2fd8e2d00e472c32edcadf5e83f6531abab","duplicate_group_id":"exact-a7d1c2fd8e2d","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"ab9ccf44dcd2c584b0e4","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_page":225,"source_qid":"3.007"}]}',0,'v2.9.4','2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z') ON CONFLICT(record_id) DO UPDATE SET source_file=excluded.source_file,source_page=excluded.source_page,domain=excluded.domain,stem=excluded.stem,options_json=excluded.options_json,source_answer=excluded.source_answer,source_explanation=excluded.source_explanation,provena