ig Section 3 — Adult Health and Aged Care
upper limbs showed numbness in the right palm and on the dorsum of the hand
extending to the middle finger. Grip strength was diminished on the right compared
to the left, and the triceps jerk on the left was normal but diminished on the right.
Magnetic resonance imaging (MRI) of the cervical spine was ordered and a sagittal
cut is illustrated. Which one of the following is the most likely diagnosis?
A. Traumatic syringomyelia affecting spinal cord at Cé.
B. Impingement radiculopathy affecting C7 nerve root.
C. Epidural haematoma of cervical spinal cord.
D. Hemisection of cervical spinal cord (Brown-Séquard syndrome).
E. ‘Clay shovellers’ injury of cervical spine.
MCQ 3.013
A 21-year-old man is hit on the left side of his face with a racquet during a game
of squash. He complains of double vision when keeping both eyes open and has
difficulty opening his mouth. Which one of the following would be the most likely
explanation of his symptoms?
A. Rupture of the globe.
B. Hyphaema affecting the left eye.
C. Fracture of the ramus of the jaw.
D. Rupture of the maxillary anirum.
E. Depressed fracture of the zygoma.
MCQ 3.014
A 21-year-old man presents with the neck swelling
illustrated, which he had noted as a slowly
enlarging, painless lump over a 12-month period.
