Magnetic resonance imaging (MRI) of the cervical spine was ordered and a sagittal
cut is illustrated. Which one of the following is the most likely diagnosis?','{"A":"Traumatic syringomyelia affecting spinal cord at Cé.","B":"Impingement radiculopathy affecting C7 nerve root.","C":"Epidural haematoma of cervical spinal cord.","D":"Hemisection of cervical spinal cord (Brown-Séquard syndrome).","E":"‘Clay shovellers’ injury of cervical spine.\nMCQ 3.013\nA 21-year-old man is hit on the left side of his face with a racquet during a game\nof squash. He complains of double vision when keeping both eyes open and has\ndifficulty opening his mouth. Which one of the following would be the most likely\nexplanation of his symptoms?\nA. Rupture of the globe.\nB. Hyphaema affecting the left eye.\nC. Fracture of the ramus of the jaw.\nD. Rupture of the maxillary anirum.\nE. Depressed fracture of the zygoma.\nMCQ 3.014\nA 21-year-old man presents with the neck swelling\nillustrated, which he had noted as a slowly\nenlarging, painless lump over a 12-month period.\nA percutaneous core biopsy reveals thyroid\nglandular tissue in a lymph node. Which one of\nthe following is the most likely diagnosis?\nA. Subacute thyroiditis.\nB. Thyroglossal duct cyst.\nC. Metastatic carcinoma of the thyroid. a\nD. Lymphadenoid goitre (Hashimoto thyroiditis). ;\nE. Lateral position of a thyroid adenoma. a\n211"}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","supporting_pages":[],"source_qid":"3.013","duplicate_group_id":"exact-ac62f90c0395","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"de904c8599602199c798","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_page":229,"source_qid":"3.013"}],"parser_version":"2.8-residual-resolver-selective-ocr-visual-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"v28_selective_ocr_base_parser","text_method":"v28_selective_ocr","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,