Section 3 — Adult Health and Aged Care
Rhabdomyosarcoma of the tongue.
Squamous cell carcinoma of the tongue.
. ‘Geographic’ tongue.
Trigeminal nerve palsy.
Hypoglossal nerve palsy.
TMOOP>
MCQ 3.018
A 20-year-old industrial worker sustains a chemical burn injury to the eyes. Which one
of the following is the most appropriate immediate first aid treatment?
Instillation of local anaesthetic.
Referral to an ophthalmologist.
Irrigation with specific neutralising agent.
Irrigation with water.
Instillation of an antibiotic.
mOOR>
MCQ 3.019
A thyrotoxic patient was subjected to subtotal thyroidectomy after she had been
made euthyroid by medical treatment. The day after the operation her temperature
is 39°C and her pulse rate 110/min and regular. She is most likely to be suffering from
which one of the following?','{"A":"Pulmonary atelectasis.","B":"Thyroid crisis.","C":"Pulmonary embolus.","D":"Wound infection.","E":". Septicaemia.\n\nAmaurosis fugax (episodes of brief monocular loss of vision) is characteristically\nassociated with which one of the following?\n\nA. Acute glaucoma.\n\nB. Ipsilateral carotid artery stenosis.\n\nC. Raised intracranial pressure.\n\nD. Systemic hypertension (>200/120 mmHg).\nE. Giant cell (temporal) arteritis.\n\nMCQ 3.021\n\nA 67-year-old man with a history of Type 2 diabetes mellitus for 11 years presents with\na deep painless ulcer over the plantar surface of the head of the third metatarsal.\nThe patient is a non-smoker and has been taking oral hypoglycaemic agents for the\npast 11 years. Which one of the following is the most likely cause of the ulcer?"}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","supporting_pages":[],"source_qid":"3.018","duplicate_group_id":"exact-7fc73a14f804","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"e2a543610e4a8f7bb451","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_page":231,"source_qid":"3.018"}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"strict_ocr_tolerant","text_method":"tesseract","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'needs_verification','[]','high','{"record_id":"e2a543610e4a8f7bb451","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_year":null,"source_page":231,"source_qid":"3.018","domain_hint":"Mixed/Unclassified","stem":"Australian Medical Council\nSection 3 — Adult Health and Aged Care\nRhabdomyosarcoma of the tongue.\nSquamous cell carcinoma of the tongue.\n. ‘Geographic’ tongue.\nTrigeminal nerve palsy.\nHypoglossal nerve palsy.\nTMOOP>\nMCQ 3.018\nA 20-year-old industrial worker sustains a chemical burn injury to the eyes. Which one\nof the following is the most appropriate immediate first aid treatment?\nInstillation of local anaesthetic.\nReferral to an ophthalmologist.\nIrrigation with specific neutralising agent.\nIrrigation with water.\nInstillation of an antibiotic.\nmOOR>\nMCQ 3.019\nA thyrotoxic patient was subjected to subtotal thyroidectomy after she had been\nmade euthyroid by medical treatment. The day after the operation her temperature\nis 39°C and her pulse rate 110/min and regular. She is most likely to be suffering from\nwhich one of the following?","options":{"A":"Pulmonary atelectasis.","B":"Thyroid crisis.","C":"Pulmonary embolus.","D":"Wound infection.","E":". Septicaemia.\n\nAmaurosis fugax (episodes of brief monocular loss of vision) is characteristically\nassociated with which one of the following?\n\nA. Acute glaucoma.\n\nB. Ipsilateral carotid artery stenosis.\n\nC. Raised intracranial pressure.\n\nD. Systemic hypertension (>200/120 mmHg).\nE. Giant cell (temporal) arteritis.\n\nMCQ 3.021\n\nA 67-year-old man with a history of Type 2 diabetes mellitus for 11 years presents with\na deep painless ulcer over the plantar surface of the head of the third metatarsal.\nThe patient is a non-smoker and has been taking oral hypoglycaemic agents for the\npast 11 years. Which one of the following is the most likely cause of the ulcer?"},"source_answer":null,"source_explanation":null,"source_answer_status":"pending_import","current_answer":null,"current_answer_status":"needs_verification","current_evidence":[],"currentness_risk":"high","currentness_keywords":["age","antibiotic","treatment"],"likely_visual_question":false,"parser_confidence":"high","parser_mode":"strict_ocr_tolerant","text_method":"tesseract","parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","stem_hash":"7fc73a14f8043737d7c5be8f1db5770fc7f607cd",