Section 3 — Adult Health and Aged Care','{"A":"Venous insufficiency.","B":"Large vessel atherosclerosis. |","C":"Infection. |","D":"Neuropathy.","E":"Presence of a foreign body. |\n\nMCQ 3.022\n\nA 25-year-old woman presents with progressive deafness over the past few months,\nworse in her right ear. She is currently pregnant with her first child at 6 months\nof gestation — her antenatal progress has so far been normal. She has had some\nassociated mild tinnitus. She has noted that she can hear better in noisy surroundings.\nHer mother also has a hearing problem.\n\nHearing tests are performed and are as follows:\n\nARinne test, comparing air conduction and bone conduction shows bone conduction\n(BC) is better than air conduction (AC) in the right ear and also in the left ear.\n\nOn a Weber test, comparing hearing in each ear when a tuning fork is placed on the\nvertex, she states that she hears the sound better in the right ear. Which one of the\nfollowing is the"}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","supporting_pages":[],"source_qid":"3.022","duplicate_group_id":"exact-9a37990b29f6","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"97753769c04030cde3a5","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_page":232,"source_qid":"3.022"},{"record_id":"8b318497c1cbb6f800a6","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_page":259,"source_qid":"3.084"},{"record_id":"2b1390f9b1c172920dcb","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_page":328,"source_qid":"3.226"}],"parser