Section 3— Adult Health and Aged Care
Chronic subdural haematoma.
Alzheimer disease.
. Wernicke encephalopathy.
Acute Addisonian crisis.
Delirium tremens.
MOO >
MCQ 3.033
he patient illustrated has presented
after sustaining a stab wound to the
back of the left forearm in a pub
brawl. He is trying to straighten his
ingers on command. Which one of
he following nerves is most likely to
have been injured?
Median nerve.
Ulnar nerve.
. Radial nerve.
Posterior interosseous nerve.
Anterior interosseous nerve.
MOOR >
MCQ 3.034
A 50-year-old man presents with a three-month history of episodes of rotatory vertigo
and dizziness, accompanied by tinnitus and progressive deafness in the left ear, with a
feeling of tightness or fullness in the ear during the attacks. The vertigo is accompanied
by vomiting and he has to lie down during an attack. Which one of the following is
the most likely cause?
A cerebellopontine angle tumour.
Méniére disease.
. Vestibular neuronitis.
Streptomycin toxicity.
Paroxysmal positional vertigo.
MOQORP>
MCQ 3.035
A patient presents with wasting of all the small muscles of one hand and sensory loss
over the medial arm and forearm. Which one of the following is likely to be the most
relevant to the diagnosis?','{"A":"The radiological demonstration of cervical spondylosis.\nA history of previous trauma of the elbow.","B":". Tenderness over the carpal tunnel.","C":"The presence of Dupuytren contractures.","D":"A history of residence in the tropics.","E":"MOQP>"}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","supporting_pages":[237],"source_qid":"3.033","duplicate_group_id":"exact-a2004def5d1e","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"fdbdf80902d88544d2b4","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_page":237,"source_qid":"3.033"}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"v27_same_page_five_structural","text_method":"tesseract","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'needs_verification','[]','medium','{"record_id":"fdbdf80902d88544d2b4","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_year":null,"source_page":237,"supporting_pages":[237],"source_qid":"3.033","domain_hint":"Mixed/Unclassified","stem":"Australian Medical Council\nSection 3— Adult Health and Aged Care\nChronic subdural haematoma.\nAlzheimer disease.\n. Wernicke encephalopathy.\nAcute Addisonian crisis.\nDelirium tremens.\nMOO >\nMCQ 3.033\nhe patient illustrated has presented\nafter sustaining a stab wound to the\nback of the left forearm in a pub\nbrawl. He is trying to straighten his\ningers on command. Which one of\nhe following nerves is most likely to\nhave been injured?\nMedian nerve.\nUlnar nerve.\n. Radial nerve.\nPosterior interosseous nerve.\nAnterior interosseous nerve.\nMOOR >\nMCQ 3.034\nA 50-year-old man presents with a three-month history of episodes of rotatory vertigo\nand dizziness, accompanied by tinnitus and progressive deafness in the left ear, with a\nfeeling of tightness or fullness in the ear during the attacks. The vertigo is accompanied\nby vomiting and he has to lie down during an attack. Which one of the following is\nthe most likely cause?\nA cerebellopontine angle tumour.\nMéniére disease.\n. Vestibular neuronitis.\nStreptomycin toxicity.\nParoxysmal positional vertigo.\nMOQORP>\nMCQ 3.035\nA patient presents with wasting of all the small muscles of one hand and sensory loss\nover the medial arm and forearm. Which one of the following is likely to be the most\nrelevant to the diagnosis?","options":{"A":"The radiological demonstration of cervical spondylosis.\nA history of previous trauma of the elbow.","B":". Tenderness over the carpal tunnel.","C":"The presence of Dupuytren contractures.","D":"A history of residence in the tropics.","E":"MOQP>"},"source_answer":null,"source_explanation":null,"source_answer_status":"pending_import","current_answer":null,"current_answer_status":"needs_verification","current_evidence":[],"currentness_risk":"medium","currentness_keywords":["age"],"likely_visual_question":false,"parser_confidence":"medium","parser_mode":"v27_same_page_five_structural","text_method":"tesseract","parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","stem_hash":"a2004def5d1e7311b415ded57edb829d830e9d3c","duplicate_group_id":"exact-a2004def5d1e","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"fdbdf80902d88544d2b4","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_page":237,"source_qid":"3.033"}]}',0,'v2.9.4','2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z') ON CONFLICT(record_id) DO UPDATE SET source_file=excluded.source_file,source_page=excluded.source_page,domain=excluded.domain,stem=excluded.stem,options_json=excluded.options_json,source_answer=excluded.source_answer,source_explana