ORR . Section 3 — Adult Health and Aged Care
MCQ 3.039
A 42-year-old carpenter complains of numbness in the little and ring fingers of his left
hand. On examination there is weakness of abduction of his little finger and weakness
of flexion of the terminal phalanx of his little and ring fingers. The appreciation of light
touch and pin prick is decreased over his ring and little fingers and the adjacent
medial border of his hand. Which one of the following is the most likely site of the
causative lesion?','{"A":"Median nerve in the forearm.","B":"Ulnar nerve at the elbow.","C":"C8 nerve root in the neck.","D":"Ulnar nerve at the wrist.","E":"Radial nerve in the spiral groove.\nMCQ 3.040\nA 45-year-old man develops weakness and wasting of the small muscles of the right\nhand. Which one of the following is least likely to be the cause?\nA. Old injury to the right elbow joint.\nB. Bronchogenic carcinoma of the right upper lobe.\nC. Multiple sclerosis.\nD. Syringomyelia.\nE. Motor neurone disease.\nMCQ 3.041\nA 40-year-old electrician complains of tremor while working. He has noticed this over\nthe past three months, since he suffered an electric shock which was not associated\nwith loss of consciousness or any evidence of injury. On examination he has no tremor\nat rest but has a fine tremor of his outstretched hands. Neurological examination is\notherwise normal. His resting pulse rate is 80/min. Which one of the following is the\nmost likely cause of his problem?\nA. Chronic anxiety.\nB. Hyperthyroidism.\nC. Parkinson disease.\nD. Benign essential tremor.\nE. Neurodegenerative reaction to electric shock.\n221\nbi"}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","supporting_pages":[],"source_qid":"3.039","duplicate_group_id":"exact-03ecbcccf9f8","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"9ffed8b4534726d4430e","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_page":239,"source_qid":"3.039"}],"parser_version":"2.8-residual-resolver-selective-ocr-visual-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"v28_selective_ocr_base_parser","text_method":"v28_selective_ocr","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,'text',NULL,'needs_verification','[]','medium','{"record_id":"9ffed8b4534726d4430e","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","