:ction 3— Adult Health and Aged Care @
MCQ 3.042
A 72-year-old man who lives alone is brought to the Emergency Department by his
daughter, who states that he is confused. On examination his speech is garbled and
difficult to follow and he gives incomprehensible answers to questions. There is no
other abnormality on examination. A computed tomography (CT) scan of the head
was performed and the relevant cuts are shown. Which one of the following is the
most likely cause of his symptoms?
: rood
SS x','{"A":"Cerebral tumour.","B":"Cerebral embolus.","C":"Cerebral infarction.","D":"Cerebral haemorrhage.","E":"Cerebral tuberculoma.\nMCQ 3.043 I\nA 25-year-old man experienced an industrial injury resulting in a Cé level quadriplegia\nten months ago. He asks you about factors affecting his life expectancy. Which one\nof the following will have the most influence on his life expectancy?\nA. His occupation before the injury.\nB. His level of physical activity before the injury.\nC. Continuing management of his neurogenic bladder.\nD. His personality and motivation.\nE. The cause of his injury.\nMCQ 3.044\nAn 80-year-old man presents complaining of loss of power in the left leg over the last\nseven days. He has a past history of Type 2 diabetes mellitus, hypertension, chronic\nbackache and osteoporosis. He is on frusemide, digoxin, alendronate, potassium\nsupplements and metformin. He had herpes zoster with a painful rash affecting the\nL2-L4 dermatomes of his left leg, two weeks ago.\nOn examination he has diminished power in the left leg affecting hip flexion and knee\nextension; the left knee jerk is diminished compared to the right. He has no sensory\nloss, and is still complaining of some burning in the L2-L4 dermatomal distribution.\nWhich one of the following is the most likely diagnosis?\ng,"}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","supporting_pages":[],"source_qid":"3.042","duplicate_group_id":"exact-436695964da3","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"08220776d682549e04ec","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_page":240,"source_qid":"3.042"}],"parser_version":"2.8-residual-resolver-selective-ocr-visual-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"v28_selective_ocr_base_parser","text_method":"v28_selective_ocr","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}'