“Section 3 - Adult Health and Aged Care
Lumbar spinal stenosis at L4-L5.
Prolapse of the L4-L5 intervertebral disc.
. Herpes zoster of the motor system.
Diabetic amyotrophy (proximal neuropathy).
Cerebrovascular (lacunar) infarction.
MOQ2>
MCQ 3.045
An 83-year-old woman was admitted to hospital 36 hours ago, following a fall causing
a fractured neck of femur. She has been living alone at home since the death of her
husband 12 months ago and was independent in self-care.
On examination she is now disoriented in time, place and person. She is agitated. An
adequate history is unobtainable. Physical examination shows the clinical features
of an intracapsular femoral neck fracture, confirmed on X-ray, and is otherwise
noncontributory. Investigations for her acute brain syndrome are as follows:
° Chest X-ray and CT scan of the brain are normal.
¢ Urea and electrolytes are normal.
¢ — Urine microscopy is normal.
¢ — Full blood examination shows
~ — *Hb 129g/L (115-165)
~ *MCV 105 fL (80-100)
~ *Platelets 80x10°/L (150-400).
¢ — Liver function tests are normal, except elevated alkaline phosphatase (ALP) and
gamma glutamy! transferase (GGT).
Which one of the following is the most likely cause of her acute delirium?
Fat embolism.
Alcohol withdrawal.
. B,, deficiency.
Hypothyroidism.
Cirrhosis of liver.
MOQR>
MCQ 3.046
A 50-year-old man with long-standing alcoholism presents with increasing abdominal
distension over the last three months associated with tense ascites. He complains also
of discomfort, pins and needles, and numbness affecting the lateral aspects of both
thighs over the same period. Which one of the following conditions is the most likely
