MCQ 3.047
A 50-year-old woman presents with a complaint of ‘jumpy legs’, with involuntary
movements and uncomfortable feelings in both legs, particularly occurring at night,
and requiring her to get up and move around, with transient relief. The symptoms
both prevent her from settling to sleep and interrupt her sleep, and have persisted
for the past 12 months. She has a past history of surgery for varicose veins and a
hysterectomy for menorrhagia, but has otherwise been in good health. She recalls
that her mother used to be troubled by similar symptoms. Which one of the following
is the most likely diagnosis?','{"A":"Nocturnal muscle cramps.","B":"Chorea (‘Saint Vitus dance’).","C":"Ischaemic rest pain.","D":"Restless legs syndrome (Ekbom syndrome).","E":"Chronic venous insufficiency (CVI)."}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","supporting_pages":[],"source_qid":"3.047","duplicate_group_id":"exact-66b15090d4b7","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"ca52dff3fb77cc862471","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_page":242,"source_qid":"3.047"}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"strict_ocr_tolerant","text_method":"tesseract","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'needs_verification','[]','low','{"record_id":"ca52dff3fb77cc862471","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_year":null,"source_page":242,"source_qid":"3.047","domain_hint":"Mixed/Unclassified","stem":"ustralian Medical Council\nMCQ 3.047\nA 50-year-old woman presents with a complaint of ‘jumpy legs’, with involuntary\nmovements and uncomfortable feelings in both legs, particularly occurring at night,\nand requiring her to get up and move around, with transient relief. The symptoms\nboth prevent her from settling to sleep and interrupt her sleep, and have persisted\nfor the past 12 months. She has a past history of surgery for varicose veins and a\nhysterectomy for menorrhagia, but has otherwise been in good health. She recalls\nthat her mother used to be troubled by similar symptoms. Which one of the following\nis the most likely diagnosis?","options":{"A":"Nocturnal muscle cramps.","B":"Chorea (‘Saint Vitus dance’).","C":"Ischaemic rest pain.","D":"Restless 