the following diagnoses? : : a','{"A":"C7 vertebral fracture. |","B":"Fracture dislocation of C1-C2 vertebrae. Dy","C":"Cervical spondylosis. a","D":"C4 nerve root compression. fm ‘ > A |","E":"Facet joint arthropathy. - aa\nMCQ 3.061 |\nA 70-year-old woman falls onto her outstretched left al\nhand and feels a crunch in her left wrist as she lands. }\nExamination reveals a deformed left wrist. The X-ray\nof this patient is shown. A circumferential plaster cast i aia\nis applied after manipulative reduction. The patient 2\nis discharged home. After 24 hours she complains of Bs F\ntingling and aching in the hand. On examination her .\nfingers are slightly swollen, are painful to move and are —\nsuffused. Which one of the following is the most appro- ;\npriate next step in management? :\nA. Re-X-ray the fracture. z\nB. Encourage more active finger exercises. :\nC. Split both sides of the plaster cylinder.\nD. Review the patient in 24 hours. ;\nE. Elevate the limb and change to a stronger\nanalgesic.\nMCQ 3.062 |\nAn 86-year-old man presents with pain in his right knee and limited walking with a\nlimp. You assess him as having degenerative arthritis of the knee and recommend\nthat he obtain a walking stick. In addition to using the stick, which one of the following\nwould be the most appropriate initial management?\nA. Orthopaedic evaluation for arthroscopy. |\nB. A gait rehabilitation program.\nC. Rest. /\nD. Support strapping for the knee. |\nE. Wheel chair for longer distances."}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","supporting_pages":[],"source_qid":"3.060","duplicate_group_id":"exact-7b4be16fcaf3","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"52f86be5803adf32b526","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_page":248,"source_qid":"3.060"}],"parser_version":"2.