of her right hand is shown. Which one of the
following is the most likely diagnosis?','{"A":"Polymyalgia rheumatica. KS","B":"Dermatomyositis.","C":"Systemic lupus erythematosus (SLE).","D":"Inclusion body myositis.","E":"Scleroderma.\nMCQ 3.069\nA 36-year-old man presents with a history of multiple joint pains and fevers over the\nprevious eight months. On examination, his BP is 180/118 mmHg. There is left foot drop\nand digital infarcts. Which one of the following investigations is most likely to lead to a\ndiagnosis of this patient’s illness?\nA. Full blood count.\nB. Blood cultures.\nC. Muscle biopsy.\nD. Random blood glucose.\nE. Examination of cerebrospinal fluid (CSF).\n233\n&"}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","supporting_pages":[],"source_qid":"3.068","duplicate_group_id":"exact-0cc6b81a4423","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"b99f87b687777738e4ac","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_page":251,"source_qid":"3.068"}],"parser_version":"2.8-residual-resolver-selective-ocr-visual-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"v28_selective_ocr_base_parser","text_method":"v28_selective_ocr","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,'text',NULL,'needs_verification','[]','low','{"record_id":"b99f87b687777738e4ac","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_year":null,"source_page":251,"source_qid":"3.068","domain_hint":"Mixed/Unclassified","stem":"oo ty eo eue eos eee Australian Medical Council\nMCQ 3.068\nA 45-year-old woman presents with fatigue\nover the past six months. She has difficulty =\nin getting up from a chair and in hanging\nout the washing. On examination, she has “\ngrade 4 weakness of the proximal muscles\nof the limbs. She has a maculopapular rash Z\nover her upper chest and back. Creatine Ni\nkinase (CK) is 570U/L (30-125). A photograph o\nof her right hand is shown. Which one of the\nfollowing is the most likely diagnosis?","options":{"A":"Polymyalgia rheumatica. KS","B":"Dermatomyositis.","C":"Systemic lupus erythematosus (SLE).","D":"Inclusion body myositis.","E":"Scleroderma.\nMCQ 3.069\nA 36-year-old man presents with a history of multiple joint pains and fevers over the\nprevious eight months. On examination, his BP is 180/118 mmHg. There is left foot drop\nand digital infarcts. Which one of the following investigations is most likely to lead to a\ndiagnosis of this patient’s illness?\nA. Full blood count.\nB. Blood cultures.\nC. Muscle biopsy.\nD. Random blood glucose.\nE. Examination of cerebrospinal fluid (CSF).\n233\n&"},"source_answer":null,"source_explanation":null,"source_answer_status":"pending_import","current_answer":null,"current_answer_status":"needs_verification","current_evidence":[],"currentness_risk":"low","currentness_keywords":[],"likely_visual_question":false,"parser_confidence":"high","parser_mode":"v28_selective_ocr_base_parser","text_method":"v28_selective_ocr","record_type":"text_mcq","options_mode":"text","parser_version":"2.8-residual-resolver-selective-ocr-visual-2026-09-22","stem_hash":"0cc6b81a442356b3d006fcd254ecd9cca2223018","duplicate_group_id":"exact-0cc6b81a4423","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"b99f87b687777738e4ac","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_page":251,"source_qid":"3.068"}]}',0,'v2.9.4','2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z') ON CONFLICT(record_id) DO UPDATE SET source_file=excluded.source_file,source_page=excluded.source_page,domain=excluded.domain,stem=excluded.stem,options_json=excluded.options_json,source_answer=excluded.source_answer,source_explanation=excluded.source_explanation,provenance_json