depression in V5 and V6. Her chest ‘ alae athe:
X-ray is illustrated. Which one of the
following is the most likely diagnosis?','{"A":"Pericardial effusion.","B":"Carcinoma of lung.","C":"Myocardial infarction.","D":"Aortic dissection.","E":"Sarcoidosis.\nMCQ 3.071\nA 57-year-old man with a forty pack-year smoking history presents with a two-month\nhistory of episodes of a gripping acute pain in either calf which often wakes him from\nsleep. To relieve the pain he gets out of bed and walks about.\nThe patient also has Type 2 non-insulin-dependent diabetes controlled by diet. Which\none of the following is the most likely diagnosis?\nA. Muscular cramps.\nB. Ischaemic rest pain.\nC. Peripheral neuropathy.\nD. Deep venous thrombosis.\nE. Intermittent claudication.\nMCQ 3.072\nA 56-year-old man presents with a six-month history of pain in his right calf. The pain is\nbrought on by walking and was initially eased when he stopped. More recently he has\nexperienced rest pain in the right leg, particularly at night. He smokes 40 cigarettes a\nday. On examination his BP is 150/100mmdg. His right femoral pulse is diminished and\nthe right dorsalis pedis pulse cannot be felt. His ankle-brachial BP index is 0.3 (normal\nratio is 1). Urinalysis is normal. Which one of the following is the most appropriate plan\nof managemente2\n235"}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","supporting_pages":[],"source_qid":"3.070","duplicate_group_id":"exact-aacb3ddb9ef5","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"89c124ae8be000ffde19","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_page":253,"source_qid":"3.070"}],"parser_version":"2.8-residual-resolver-selective-ocr-visual-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"v28_selective_ocr_base_parser","text_method":"v28_selective_ocr","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,'text',NULL,'needs_verification','[]','high','{"record_id"