MCQ 3.076
A 28-year-old man has had eight episodes of palpitations associated with mild
dizziness and sweating over the past year. These came on suddenly, usually after
exercise, and have lasted between 10 and 20 minutes, often stopping after putting
his face in cold water. He now presents with an attack that has been going for 2 hours
and he is mildly distressed. His ECG is shown. Which one of the following therapeutic
