moQe>
MCQ 3.079
Hypertension is the most important preventable risk factor for which one of the
following disorders?','{"A":"Coronary artery disease.","B":"Peripheral arterial disease.","C":"Renal arterial disease.","D":"Ischaemic stroke.","E":"Atrial fibrillation.\n\nMCQ 3.080\n\nA patient with aortic stenosis has had a heart catheterisation. You are told that the\naortic systolic gradient is 55mmHg. Which one of the following additional pieces of\ninformation is necessary to determine the significance of the gradient?\n\nPresence of coronary artery disease.\nLeft ventricular ejection fraction.\n\n. Left ventricular end-diastolic pressure.\nCardiac output.\n\nLeft atrial pressure.\n\nHS A @ ie ake"}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","supporting_pages":[],"source_qid":"3.077","duplicate_group_id":"exact-c582ee418041","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"9b0b52cd5ba6398d2e6a","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_page":257,"source_qid":"3.077"}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"strict_ocr_tolerant","text_method":"tesseract","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'needs_verification','[]','high','{"record_id":"9b0b52cd5ba6398d2e6a","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_year":null,"source_page":257,"source_qid":"3.077","domain_hint":"Mixed/Unclassified","stem":"Australian Medical Council\nAdult Health and Aged Care |\nMCQ 3.077\nPatients with a variety of cardiac conditions may require special care in pregnancy.\nWhich one of the following heart lesions present during pregnancy is most likely to\ncause problems?\n. Mitral stenosis.\nTricuspid regurgitation.\n. Mitral regurgitation.\n. Aortic regurgitation.\nVentricular septal defect.\nBe) (o) (Oyo. >\nMCQ 3.078\nIn which one of the following conditions would silent painless myocardial infarction\nbe most common?\n. Polycythaemia vera.\nHypertension.\n. Diabetes.\n. Migraine.\nHypercholesterolaemia.\nmoQe>\nMCQ 3.079\nHypertension is the most important preventable risk factor for which one of the\nfollowing disorders?","options":{"A":"Coronary artery disease.","B":"Peripheral arterial disease.","C":"Renal arterial disease.","D":"Ischaemic stroke.","E":"Atrial fibrillation.\n\nMCQ 3.080\n\nA patient with aortic stenosis has had a heart catheterisation. You are told that the\naortic systolic gradient is 55mmHg. Which one of the following additional pieces of\ninformation is necessary to determine the significance of the gradient?\n\nPresence of coronary artery disease.\nLeft ventricular ejection fraction.\n\n. Left ventricular end-diastolic pressure.\nCardiac output.\n\nLeft atrial pressure.\n\nHS A @ ie ake"},"source_answer":null,"source_explanation":null,"source_answer_status":"pending_import","current_answer":null,"current_answer_status":"needs_verification","current_evidence":[],"currentness_risk":"high","currentness_keywords":["age","diabetes","hypertension","pregnan"],"likely_visual_question":false,"parser_confidence":"high","parser_mode":"strict_ocr_tolerant","text_method":"tesseract","parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","stem_hash":"c582ee4180418e90270ce0d6cc425424da18cfde","duplicate_group_id":"exact-c582ee418041","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"9b0b52cd5ba6398d2e6a","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_page":257,"source_qid":"3.077"}]}',0,'v2.9.4','2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z') ON CONFLICT(record_id) DO UPDATE SET source_file=excluded.source_file,source_page=excluded.source_page,domain=excluded.domain,stem=excluded.stem,options_json=excluded