Section 3 — Adult Health and Aged Care
. Prescribe an oral broad spectrum antibiotic and review in one month with repeat
chest X-ray.
B. Await sputum culture results before deciding on further management.
C. Perform bronchoscopy to obtain further specimens for smear and culture of
possible acid-fast bacilli before deciding on future management.
D. Commence anti-tuberculous treatment without delay.
E. Arrange followup chest X-ray and review in three months.
MCQ 3.092
A 30-year-old man presents to the emergency department complaining of a dry
cough, fever, dyspnoea and diarrhoea which began three days after the onset of
an upper respiratory tract infection. On physical examination his respiratory rate is 20/
min, temperature 40.5°C and the chest shows bibasal inspiratory crackles. Chest X-ray
shows bilateral interstitial infiltrates. Initial antimicrobial therapy should be which one
of the following?
Penicillin.
Azithromycin.
. Ciprofloxacin.
High dose trimethoprim-sulphamethoxazole.
Amoxycillin/clavulinic acid.
MOQF>
MCQ 3.093
Which one of the following sets of symptoms would best fit a diagnosis of lower limb
ischaemia related to major vessel atherosclerotic thrombotic occlusion?','{"A":"Sudden onset of pain in the calf.","B":"Gradual onset of paralysis in the calf and foot.","C":"Pain in the buttocks brought on by walking and relieved by recumbency.","D":"Shooting pain down the posterior aspect of the thigh and leg.","E":"Nocturnal rest pain partly relieved by leg dependency.\n\nMCQ 3.094\n\nA patient with a crush injury of the anterior chest, with bilateral fractures of multiple ribs\nwith paradoxical ventilation, is best initially treated by which one of the following?\n\nA. Thoracotomy and internal fixation.\n\nB. Strapping of the chest to prevent flailing.\n\nC. Immobilisation by external fixation.\n\nD. Intubation and controlled ventilation and insertion of intercostal catheters.\nE. Pressure support, such as with sandbags, to prevent flailing."}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","supporting_pages":[],"source_qid":"3.092","duplicate_group_id":"exact-54bc910692c7","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"1ced90c653d6f9b4baf0","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_page":263,"source_qid":"3.092"}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"strict_ocr_tolerant","text_method":"tesseract","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'needs_verification','[]','high','{"record_id":"1ced90c653d6f9b4baf0","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_year":null,"source_page":263,"source_qid":"3.092","domain_hint":"Mixed/Unclassified","stem":"Australian Medical Council\nSection 3 — Adult Health and Aged Care\n. Prescribe an oral broad spectrum antibiotic and review in 