 The patient is normally in good health and has\nnever had this pain before. He smokes 20 cigarettes a day. A recent routine check\nshowed his cholesterol was marginally elevated. Which one of the following would be\nthe most likely explanation for his symptoms?\nA. A perforated peptic ulcer.\nB. An inferior myocardial infarction.\nC. Biliary colic.\nD. Acute pancreatitis.\nE. Aruptured abdominal aortic aneurysm.\nMCQ 3.097\nA 55-year-old man presents with a six-month history of increasing dysphagia for solid\nfood. He has a previous history, going back over many years, of gastro-oesophageal\nreflux. He has managed his reflux with antacids but, since the dysphagia started,\nhis reflux has not been so troublesome. Which one of the following is the most likely\ndiagnosis?\nA. Carcinoma of the oesophagus.\nB. Achalasia of the oesophagus.\nC. Peptic oesophageal stricture.\nD. Paraoesophageal hernia.\nE. Ulcerative oesophagitis.\n247"},"source_answer":null,"source_explanation":null,"source_answer_status":"pending_import","current_answer":null,"current_answer_status":"needs_verification","current_evidence":[],"currentness_risk":"medium","currentness_keywords":["age"],"likely_visual_question":false,"parser_confidence":"high","parser_mode":"v28_selective_ocr_base_parser","text_method":"v28_selective_ocr","record_type":"text_mcq","options_mode":"text","parser_version":"2.8-residual-resolver-selective-ocr-visual-2026-09-22","stem_hash":"bbd75ffdcaaabb955dd28cea398b7a89882e35a3","duplicate_group_id":"exact-bbd75ffdcaaa","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"87519b110af68f04a3be","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_page":265,"source_qid":"3.095"}]}',0,'v2.9.4','2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z') ON CONFLICT(record_id) DO UPDATE SET source_file=excluded.source_file,source_page=excluded.source_page,domain=excluded.domain,stem=exc