description?','{"A":"Isolated metastatic deposit.","B":"Haemangioma. |","C":"Hepatocellular carcinoma.","D":"Liver cyst. |","E":"Hydatid cyst. |\nMCQ 3.099\nThe photograph is one of a barium swallow series (showing the |\nupper and mid oesophagus) that has been performed in a\n75-year-old man. He presented with symptoms that had been :\npresent for 12 months. Which one of the following symptoms -\nwould have been the most likely mode of presentation?\nA. Recurrent chest infection.\nB. Progressive loss of weight.\nC. A retrosternal burning sensation. \\\nD. Gurgling in the neck. se\nE. Regurgitation of food. al\nMCQ 3.100 |\nA previously well 32-year-old woman is admitted with a two-day history of colicky\ngeneralised abdominal pain, which has shifted and become constant in the right\niliac fossa. On examination she looks unwell, has a temperature of 38.1°C and has\nmarked tenderness, guarding and release tenderness in the right iliac fossa. Which\none of the following is the most appropriate management option?\nA. Start a course of intravenous antibiotics and review after several hours.\nB. Arrange for a computed tomogram (CT) of the abdomen.\nC. Arrange an ultrasound examination of the lower abdomen and pelvis.\nD. Arrange for a gynaecological consultation.\nE. Book the patient for emergency surgery.\n\n|"}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","supporting_pages":[],"source_qid":"3.098","duplicate_group_id":"exact-ee831648684f","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"f52bfc8d004af76c59c1","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_page":266,"source_qid":"3.098"}],"parser_version":"2.8-residual-resolver-selective-ocr-visual-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"v28_selective_ocr_base_parser","text_method":"v28_selective_ocr","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":n