Mee eo Se Section 3 - Adult Health and Aged Care
MCQ 3.101
A 45-year-old man is diagnosed with a primary lymphoma of the small bowel. In
checking for predisposing factors, which one of the following risk factors is most likely
to be present?','{"A":"Crohn disease.","B":"Peutz-Jeghers syndrome.","C":"Coeliac disease.","D":"Familial adenomatous polyposis.","E":"Previous gastrectomy.\nMCQ 3.102\nA 50-year-old man who smokes forty cigarettes a day had his right inguinal hernia\nrepaired under general anaesthetic. Twenty-four hours after surgery he developed a\nfever of 37.8°C. Which one of the following is the most likely cause of the fever?\nA. Wound infection.\nB. Wound haematoma.\nC. Prostatitis.\nD. Pulmonary atelectasis.\nE. Epididymitis.\nMCQ 3.103\nA 35-year-old homosexual man presented with a six-month history of fatigue. He had\nnever been jaundiced. Laboratory tests of liver function showed the following results.\nBilirubin 15umol/L — (<20)\nAlbumin 35g/L (32-45)\nAspartate aminotransferase (AST) *100IU/L (<40)\nAlanine aminotransferase (ALT) 80IU/L (<35)\nHBsAg positive\nA liver biopsy showed chronic hepatitis. He now presents for counselling. Which one\nof the following would be the most appropriate advice?\nA. As he is not jaundiced, no followup is required.\nB. He should be treated with prednisolone.\nC. His contacts should be given normal human immunoglobulin.\nD. He is at significant risk of developing hepatocellular carcinoma.\nE. He has less than a 5% chance of developing cirrhosis of the liver.\n249\nke"}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","supporting_pages":[],"source_qid":"3.101","duplicate_group_id":"exact-35f97c105d56","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"9e95954e0c6c400f0242","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_page":267,"source_qid":"3.101"}],"parser_version":"2.8-residual-resolver-selective-ocr-visual-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"v28_selective_ocr_base_parser","text_method":"v28_selective_ocr","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,