eZ : Section 3 - Adult Health and Aged Care','{"A":"A dilated, thickened gallbladder containing stones.","B":"Normal liver parenchyma with a normal intrahepatic biliary tree.","C":"A dilated intrahepatic and extrahepatic biliary system.","D":"A dilated pancreatic duct and normal common bile duct.","E":"A dilated common bile duct and normal intrahepatic bile ducts.\nMCQ 3.108\nA 17-year-old youth presents with a swelling in the right groin which has been present\nfor only one month. On palpation, the swelling is felt over the external inguinal ring\naccompanied by an impulse on coughing, but disappears when lying down. The\nother groin feels normal. Scrotal examination is normal in the supine and erect\npositions. Which one of the following is the most appropriate advice?\nA. Proceed to surgical repair.\nB. Abdominal wall ultrasound to clarify the diagnosis.\nC. Review in one month''s time.\nD. Ultrasound-guided fine needle aspiration cytology (FNAC).\nE. Ultrasound-guided sclerotherapy.\nMCQ 3.109\nA 65-year-old man presents with a three-month history of the passage of blood and\nmucus mixed in with his faeces. He has never had these symptoms before. Which one\nof the following conditions is the most likely diagnosis?\nA. Ulcerative colitis.\nB. Ischaemic colitis.\nC. Diverticular disease of the sigmoid colon.\nD. Carcinoma of the colon.\nE. Internal haemorrhoids.\nMCQ 3.110\nA 35-year-old Caucasian woman is admitted with a haematemesis. On examination\nshe has a BP of 95/60mmHg and a pulse of 100/min. She appears reasonably well\nnourished. Her sclerae are yellow and she has scratch marks and bruises on her arms.\nHer abdomen is distended and soft with evidence of shifting dullness. Dilated veins\nare easily visible in the subcutaneous tissues and the liver is palpable three finger-\nbreadths below the costal margin. Which one of the following is the most likely underlying\ncause for her problem?\nA. Alcoholic liver disease.\nB. Biliary cirrhosis.\nC. Schistosomiasis.\nD. Budd-Chiari syndrome.\nE. Hepatitis C cirrhosis.\n251"}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","supporting_pages":[],"source_qid":"3.108","duplicate_group_id":"exact-993028c9aa82","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"bccfb1dd1c76bb759def","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_page":269,"source_qid":"3.108"}],"parser_version":"2.8-residual-resolver-selective-ocr-visual-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"v28_selective_ocr_base_parser","text_method":"v28_selective_ocr","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,'text',NULL,'needs_verification','[]','medium','{"record_id":"bccfb1dd1c76bb759def","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_year":null,"source_page":269,"source_qid":"3.108","domain_hint":"Mixed/Unclassified","stem":"ee : aR eae ae Australian Medical Council\neZ : Section 3 - Adult Health and Aged Care","options":{"A":"A dilated, thickened gallbladder containing stones.","B":"Normal liver parenchyma with a normal intrahepatic biliary tree.","C":"A dilated intrahepatic and extrahepatic biliary system.","D":"A dilated pancreatic duct and normal common bile duct.","E":"A dilated common bile duct and normal intrahepatic bile ducts.\nMCQ 3.108\nA 17-year-old youth presents with a swelling in the right groin which has been present\nfor only one month. On palpation, the swelling is felt over the external inguinal ring\naccompanied by an impulse on coughing, but disappears when lying down. The\nother groin feels normal. Scrotal examination is normal in the supine and erect\npositions. Which one of the following is the most appropriate advice?\nA. Proceed to surgical repair.\nB. Abdominal wall ultrasound to clarify the diagnosis.\nC. Review in one month''s time.\nD. Ultrasound-guided fine needle aspiration cytology (FNAC).\nE. Ultrasound-guided sclerotherapy.\nMCQ 3.109\nA 65-year-old man presents with a three-month history of the passage of blood and\nmucus mixed in with his faeces. He has never had these symptoms before. Which one\nof the following conditions is the most likely diagnosis?\nA. Ulcerative colitis.\nB. Ischaemic colitis.\nC. Diverticular disease of the sigmoid colon.\nD. Carcinoma of the colon.\nE. Internal haemorrhoids.\nMCQ 3.110\nA 35-year-old Caucasian woman is admitted with a haematemesis. On examination\nshe has a BP of 95/60mmHg and a pulse of 100/min. She appears reasonably well\nnourished. Her sclerae are yellow and she has scratch marks and bruises on her arms.\nHer abdomen is distended and soft with evidence of shifting dullness. Dilated veins\nare easily visible in the subcutaneous tissues and the liver is palpable three finger-\nbreadths below the costal margin. Which one of the following is the most likely underlying\ncause for her problem?\nA. Alcoholic liver disease.\nB. Biliary cirrhosis.\nC. Schistosomiasis.\nD. Budd-Chiari syndrome.\nE. Hepatitis C cirrhosis.\n251"},"source_answer":null,"source_explanation":null,"source_answer_status":"pending_import","current_answer":null,"current_answer_status":"needs_verification","current_evidence":[],"currentness_risk":"medium","currentness_keywords":["age"],"likely_visual_question":false,"parser_confidence":"high","parser_mode":"v28_selective_ocr_base_parser","text_method":"v28_selective_ocr","record_type":"text_mcq","options_mode":"text","parser_version":"2.8-residual-resolver-selective-ocr-visual-2026-09-22","stem_hash":"993028c9aa82f8aa8863c855f2ee89e7007b8575","duplicate_group_id":"exact-993028c9aa82","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"bccfb1dd1c76bb759def","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Hand