ection 3 — Adult Health and Aged Care
MCQ 3.111
An 83-year-old man attends the Emergency Department .
with a two-day history of cramping abdominal pain,
distension and vomiting. He has absolute constipation. The
patient is normally bed-bound in a nursing home. The past .
medical history includes a laparotomy for appendicitis. He }
is on medication for Parkinson disease. The plain abdominal
radiograph is shown. Which one of the following is the most :
likely underlying cause of the problem?','{"A":"Carcinoma of the sigmoid colon. \"","B":"Sigmoid volvulus. ’","C":"Faecal impaction. > lal .","D":"Drug-induced pseudo-obstruction.","E":"Adhesion-obstruction.\nMCQ 3.112\nAn otherwise fit 57-year-old woman spikes a temperature of 39°C five days after an\nappendicectomy for acute appendicitis. There is a tender, reddened and fluctuant\nswelling at the medial end of the wound. Which one of the following would be the\nmost appropriate next step in management?\nA. Administer high dose, broad spectrum, intravenous antibiotics.\nB. Return the patient to theatre for resuturing of the wound.\nC. Place the patient on oral antibiotics.\nD. Make an incision over the swelling to allow free drainage.\nE. Remove the underlying suture material to prevent sinus formation.\nMCQ 3.113 |\nA Meckel embryologic remnant in the small bowel can present in a number of different )\nways. Which one of the following would be the most common mode of presentation?\nA. Discharge from the umbilicus.\nB. Acute small bowel obstruction.\nC. Acute gastrointestinal haemorrhage. |\nD. Incidental finding at operation.\nE. Tiredness due to chronic blood loss.\nMCQ 3.114\nAn 81-year-old man undergoes a laparotomy for perforated diverticular disease\nand peritonitis. A Hartmann procedure (sigmoid colectomy and end colostomy with\noversewing of distal stump) is performed. Postoperatively he develops a paralytic\nileus with abdominal distension and the colostomy does not begin to function until\nday six. At day seven he develops a small superficial wound infection which is treated\nby removing two skin staples. Two days later he suffers a complete disruption of the\nabdominal wound. As he is taken to the operating room for repair of the wound, it\nis noticed that the haemoglobin is 110g/L (130-180) and the serum albumin is 30g/L\n(32-45). )\n——_ — 4"}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","supporting_pages":[],"source_qid":"3.111","duplicate_group_id":"exact-c9f31d3c3f4e","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"3980db4d1e8ad01a2731","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_page":270,"source_qid":"3.111"}],"parser_version":"2.8-residual-resolver-selective-ocr-visual-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"v28_selective_ocr_base_parser","text_method":"v28_selective_ocr","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,'text',NULL,'needs_verification','[]','medium','{"record_id":"3980db4d1e8ad01a2731","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_year":null,"source_page":270,"source_qid":"3.111","domain_hint":"Mixed/Unclassified","stem":"ustralian Medical Council ?\nection 3 — Adult Health and Aged Care\nMCQ 3.111\nAn 83-year-old man attends the Emergency Department .\nwith a two-day history of cramping abdominal pain,\ndistension and vomiting. He has absolute constipation. The\npatient is normally bed-bound in a nursing home. The past .\nmedical history includes a laparotomy for appendicitis. He }\nis on medication for Parkinson disease. The plain abdominal\nradiograph is shown. Which one of the following is the most :\nlikely underlying cause of the problem?","options":{"A":"Carcinoma of the sigmoid colon. \"","B":"Sigmoid volvulus. ’","C":"Faecal impaction. > lal .","D":"Drug-induced pseudo-obstruction.","E":"Adhesion-obstruction.\nMCQ 3.112\nAn otherwise fit 57-year-old woman spikes a temperature of 39°C five days after an\nappendicectomy for acute appendicitis. There is a tender, reddened and fluctuant\nswelling at the medial end of the wound. Which one of the following would be the\nmost appropriate next step in management?\nA. Administer high dose, broad spectrum, intravenous antibiotics.\nB. Return the patient to theatre for resuturing of the wound.\nC. Place the patient on oral antibiotics.\nD. Make an incision over the swelling to allow free drainage.\nE. Remove the underlying suture material to prevent sinus formation.\nMCQ 3.113 |\nA Meckel embryologic remnant in the small bowel can present in a number of different )\nways. Which one of the following would be the most common mode of presentation?\nA. Discharge from the umbilicus.\nB. Acute small bowel obstruction.\nC. Acute gastrointestinal haemorrhage. |\nD. Incidental finding at operation.\nE. Tiredness due to chronic blood loss.\nMCQ 3.114\nAn 81-year-old man undergoes a laparotomy for perforated diverticular disease\nand peritonitis. A Hartmann procedure (sigmoid colectomy and end colostomy with\noversewing of distal stump) is performed. Postoperatively he develops a paralytic\nileus with abdominal distension and the colostomy does not begin to function until\nday six. At day seven he develops a small superficial wound infection which is treated\nby removing two skin staples. Two days later he suffers a complete disruption of the\nabdominal wound. As he is taken to the operating room for repair of the wound, it\nis noticed that the haemoglobin is 110g/L (130-180) and the serum albumin is 30g/L\n(32-45). )\n——_ — 4"},"source_answer":null,"source_explanation":null,"source_answer_status":"pending_import","current_answer":null,"current_answer_status":"needs_verification","current_evidence":[],"currentness_risk":"medium","currentness_keywords":["age"],"likely_visual_question":true,"parser_confidence":"high","parser_mode":"v28_selective_ocr_base_parser","text_method":"v28_selective_ocr","record_type":"text_mcq","options_mode":"text","parser_version":"2.8-residual-resolver-selective-ocr-visual-2026-09-22","stem_hash":"c9f31d3c3f4eef064866b88750d74c1990508fcd","duplicate_group_id":"exact-c9f31d3c3f4e","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"3980db4d1e8ad01a2731","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_page":270,"source_qid":"3.111"}]}',0,'v2.9.4','2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z') ON CONFLICT(record_id) DO UPDATE SET source_file=excluded.source_file,source_page=excluded.source_page,domain=excluded.domain,stem=excluded.stem,options_json=excluded.options_json,source_answer=excluded.source_answer,source_explanation=excluded.source_explanation,provenance_json=excluded.provenance_json,visual_asset=excluded.visual_asset,visual_url=excluded.visual_url,options_mode=excluded.options_mode,current_answer=excluded.current_answer,current_answer_status=excluded.current_answer_status,current_evidence_json=excluded.current_evidence_json,currentness_risk=excluded.currentness_risk,record_json=excluded.record_json,active_quiz=excluded.active_quiz,import_version=excluded.import_version,imported_at=excluded.imported_at;
