Erect film Supine film','{"A":"Metastatic intraperitoneal carcinoma.","B":"Abdominal adhesions.","C":"Gallstone ileus.","D":"Carcinoma of the right colon.","E":"Abdominal lymphosarcoma.\n\nMCQ 3.122\n\nA 45-year-old man with a history of alcoholic cirrhosis with hepatosplenomegaly\n\npresents after vomiting fresh blood on four occasions. He is sweating, pulse is 120/\n\nmin, BP 100/60mmHg, dropping to 85/40mmHg on sitting up. After haemodynamic\n\nstabilisation of the patient, which one of the following is the most important diagnostic\n\nprocedure?\n\nA. Abdominal computed tomography (CT).\n\nB. Upper gastrointestinal endoscopy.\n\nC. Triple phase CT to view the portal circulation.\n\nD. Coeliac axis angiography.\n\nE. Transjugular intrahepatic portal venography.\n\n255"}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","supporting_pages":[],"source_qid":"3.122","duplicate_group_id":"exact-b4c0bebfe161","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"a324f0340d412941ee5f","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_page":273,"source_qid":"3.122"}],"parser_version":"2.8-residual-resolver-selective-ocr-visual-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"v28_selective_ocr_base_parser","text_method":"v28_selective_ocr","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,'text',NULL,'needs_verification','[]','medium','{"record_id":"a324f0340d412941ee5f","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_year":null,"source_page":273,"source_qid":"3.122","domain_hint":"Mixed/Unclassified","stem":"[ Australian Medical Council\nF Section 3 — Adult Health and Aged Care\nA. aaa tae\n- 7 ,\nBe “a a fe ae\nie . Te \" at ace a A ine\n@ 9 ry\nErect film Supine film","options":{"A